@startuml qnx_dispatch_server_input_activity
title QnxDispatchServer - request and one-way input dispatch

start
:Enter accepted ServerConnection::ProcessInput(code, borrowed payload);
:Recover the server and dereference user_data_;
if (Code is REQUEST?) then (yes)
    if (UserData holds a handler unique pointer?) then (handler)
        :Invoke handler->OnMessageSentWithReply(connection, payload);
    else (server callback)
        :Invoke server.sent_with_reply_callback_(connection, payload);
    endif
    :Return the callback result's has_value();
    stop
else (other code)
    :Inspect the remaining code;
endif
if (Code is SEND?) then (yes)
    if (UserData holds a handler unique pointer?) then (handler)
        :Invoke handler->OnMessageSent(connection, payload);
    else (server callback)
        :Invoke server.sent_callback_(connection, payload);
    endif
    :Return the callback result's has_value();
    stop
else (unknown)
    :Return false;
endif
stop

legend
    Native input dispatch runs on the server worker in the shown engine path.
    Routing uses the current variant type, not a separate stored mode.
    No null-handler or empty-server-callback guard is added.
    The payload remains borrowed from native request storage.
    The engine currently discards this boolean in io_write:
    false does not itself close the connection or send an application error.
endlegend

@enduml
